# Outflow AI — Phase 1

## Execution Core MVP

**Duration:** 6 Weeks
**Objective:** Build a production-ready, persistent, async execution engine for visual workflows.

---

# Phase 1 Outcome

By the end of Phase 1:

* Pipelines persist in PostgreSQL
* Pipelines execute deterministically
* Execution runs are stored and queryable
* Runtime logic is modular (registry-based)
* Execution engine is fully async-ready
* Validation layer is structured and extensible
* Frontend supports execution inspection

This phase builds the core infrastructure for future AI-agent orchestration.

---

# 1. Pipeline Persistence Layer

## Goals

* Store pipelines in PostgreSQL
* Enable CRUD operations
* Allow frontend to load/save pipelines

## 🗄 Database: pipelines

| Field      | Type      |
| ---------- | --------- |
| id         | UUID (PK) |
| name       | VARCHAR   |
| nodes      | JSONB     |
| edges      | JSONB     |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMP |

## 🔌 Required Endpoints

* [ ] POST `/pipelines`
* [ ] GET `/pipelines`
* [ ] GET `/pipelines/{id}`
* [ ] PUT `/pipelines/{id}`
* [ ] DELETE `/pipelines/{id}`

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Pipelines survive server restarts
* [ ] Frontend can load saved pipelines
* [ ] Pipelines can be renamed and updated

---

# 2. Execution Engine Refactor

## Goals

Replace monolithic execution logic with a layered architecture.

## Required Architecture

```
Execution Service
    ├── Graph Validator
    ├── Topological Resolver
    ├── Runtime Registry
    ├── Execution Context
    └── Result Aggregator
```

## ExecutionContext

* [ ] run_id
* [ ] pipeline_id
* [ ] node_results (dict)
* [ ] logs (list)
* [ ] status (running/success/failure)

## Runtime Registry Pattern

* [ ] Implement NODE_REGISTRY mapping
* [ ] Create BaseRuntime interface
* [ ] Implement runtime classes per node type
* [ ] Remove large if/else execution blocks

### Runtime Interface

```python
class BaseRuntime:
    async def execute(self, node, inputs, context):
        pass
```

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Adding a new node type requires only a new runtime class
* [ ] Execution engine has no monolithic branching
* [ ] Clear separation of concerns

---

# 3. Async Execution Conversion

## Goals

Make execution engine async-ready.

## Required

* [ ] Convert FastAPI endpoints to async
* [ ] Make runtime execute() async
* [ ] Ensure non-blocking I/O
* [ ] Support awaited LLM/API calls (mocked initially)

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] No blocking operations in execution path
* [ ] Ready for real LLM integrations

---

# 4. Execution Logging & Observability

## Goals

Provide structured execution results per node.

## Execution Result Schema

```json
{
  "run_id": "uuid",
  "status": "success",
  "node_results": {
    "node-1": {
      "status": "success",
      "duration_ms": 12,
      "output": {}
    }
  }
}
```

## Required Per Node

* [ ] start_time
* [ ] end_time
* [ ] duration_ms
* [ ] status
* [ ] output
* [ ] error (if exists)

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Failed nodes return structured errors
* [ ] Execution does not crash entire pipeline
* [ ] Logs are accessible for debugging

---

# 5. Execution Run History

## Database: execution_runs

| Field       | Type      |
| ----------- | --------- |
| id          | UUID (PK) |
| pipeline_id | UUID (FK) |
| status      | VARCHAR   |
| results     | JSONB     |
| started_at  | TIMESTAMP |
| finished_at | TIMESTAMP |

## Required Endpoints

* [ ] POST `/pipelines/{id}/execute`
* [ ] GET `/pipelines/{id}/runs`
* [ ] GET `/runs/{run_id}`

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Every execution creates a stored run
* [ ] Runs can be queried later
* [ ] Results are replayable

---

# 6. Graph Validation Layer

## Goals

Expand validation beyond DAG detection.

## Required Validations

* [ ] Cycle detection
* [ ] Orphan node detection
* [ ] Required input enforcement
* [ ] Type compatibility validation
* [ ] Multiple root validation

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Invalid pipelines cannot execute
* [ ] Error messages are descriptive
* [ ] Validation errors returned as structured responses

---

# 7. Frontend Execution Inspector

## Goals

Replace alert-based execution feedback with visual inspector.

## 🛠 Required UI Features

* [ ] Execution order display
* [ ] Per-node output viewer
* [ ] Node duration display
* [ ] Error highlighting in graph
* [ ] Failed node visual indicators

## Acceptance Criteria

* [ ] Users can inspect intermediate outputs
* [ ] Errors are clearly visible
* [ ] Execution feels interactive and debuggable

